       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for a prescription adult dose of 3,200 mg/day, and well above the OTC limit of 1,200 mg/day. At that dose the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up sharply, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common anti-inflammatory regimen\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum dose\n- **1600 mg/day total**, divided differently\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg QID, tell me and add a note about the clinical rationale. I'll enter it as written with that note. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
      }
